    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll**, who represent our highest-ceiling plays at 76.14 and 72.02, respectively. **James Wood** earns his top spot facing Burrows with a soft 4.71 xERA and a scorching .425 xwOBA, bolstered significantly by the leadoff spot and a 17% SP skill efficiency bump. **Corbin Carroll** remains a critical anchor for our stolen base objectives; despite a moderate park factor, the elite sprint speed profile against Buehler ensures he maintains high efficiency. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** provides the most reliable power-to-matchup ratio of the day, as a 14% SP skill advantage against Mikolas (4.59 xERA) and an elevated spot in the order push his score to a strong 68.21.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, most notably the bottom of the order. **Dalton Rushing** sits at a marginal 41.12, suppressed by a L/L platoon disadvantage against Freeland and a suboptimal nine-hole assignment, though his raw talent keeps him in the starting mix. **Jose Caballero** also faces a tough day with a score of 45.22, largely due to a 13% penalty in his platoon dynamic against Jax. Interestingly, **Austin Riley** narrowly avoids being the most interesting \"bench\" candidate; he lands at 59.30\u2014the highest of our marginal plays\u2014benefiting from a slight bump in SB potential due to Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which arguably saved him from a benching in favor of rest days for the inactive **Josh Naylor** or **Seiya Suzuki**.\n\nLooking forward, we are managing game caps aggressively with our bench depth. While **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, we continue to monitor the utility roles held by **Max Muncy** and **Zach McKinstry** to ensure we don't bleed at-bats against elite arms. We are optimistic that the offensive momentum from **Kyle Karros**\u2014who enjoys a massive 19% SP skill advantage and a favorable platoon spot today\u2014will provide the necessary cover for our lower-scoring middle infielders. Keep a close watch on **Brice Turang**; while his efficiency score of 55.58 is impacted by a 4% penalty for facing a high-SB-suppression environment, his base speed metrics remain a focal point for our roster strategy.",
